{"kind":"request","text":"Terminate the git-fetch positional so --remote cannot inject options or a transport (finding #2 of the 2026-08-11 security assessment at main 8f22ba52; re-verify at the implementation head). fetchSequenceRefs (cmd/gs/main.go:1638-1655) passes the operator-supplied remote as a bare positional to `git fetch --atomic --no-tags \u003cremote\u003e \u003crefspec\u003e` with no `--` and no validation, and first writes remote.\u003cremote\u003e.fetch config. Because a named remote with a fetch refspec but no url is treated by git as a URL alias, --remote 'ext::sh -c \"...\"' is handed to git's ext transport and executed (RCE); a leading '-' is parsed as a git fetch option. The same file already guards other call sites (canonicalCommit uses --end-of-options at :816; merge uses -- at :451). This matters in the agent-driven model where a --remote value can be influenced by untrusted workroom/issue text. Direction: validate the remote name (reject leading '-' and transport prefixes) before both the config write and the fetch, and/or terminate the fetch positional with --.","body":{"conditions":"gs attach rejects or safely terminates a --remote value beginning with '-' or naming a transport (ext::, file://, etc.), so neither option-injection nor ext:: execution is reachable; the git fetch positional is protected; a test covers a hostile --remote; make test and make race pass; request/ branch, independent review at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 8f22ba52; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}